From: Chiel Prins <chiel@cpeb.it>
Subject: [PATCH] rkflash: include linux/string.h for memset()

sfc_nor.c calls memset() without including <linux/string.h>. GCC used to
let that through with a warning, but GCC 14 makes an implicit function
declaration an error, so the driver no longer builds:

  drivers/rkflash/sfc_nor.c:574:9: error: implicit declaration of
  function 'memset' [-Werror=implicit-function-declaration]

Signed-off-by: Chiel Prins <chiel@cpeb.it>
---
--- a/drivers/rkflash/sfc_nor.c	2026-09-18 17:17:37.081815652 +0200
+++ b/drivers/rkflash/sfc_nor.c	2026-09-18 17:17:37.126825263 +0200
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #include <linux/bug.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
+#include <linux/string.h>
 
 #include "rkflash_debug.h"
 #include "sfc_nor.h"
